  "body": {
    "id": "lem:grid-randomization-bound",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(n,M\\) and every interior \\(q\\),\n\\[\n0\\leq\\Lambda_{n,M}^{\\mathrm{all}}-G_n^{\\mathrm{all}}\n\\leq\\frac1{4M^2},\n\\qquad\n0\\leq\\Lambda_{n,M}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q)-G_n^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q)\n\\leq\\frac1{4M^2}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "M",
      "q",
      "\\Lambda_{n,M}^{\\mathrm{all}}",
      "G_n^{\\mathrm{all}}",
      "\\Lambda_{n,M}^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q)",
      "G_n^{\\mathrm{iid}}(q)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:orbit-games",
      "def:grid-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Restricting actions cannot lower either minimax value, proving the two left inequalities.  Conversely, for any action \\(d\\in[-1,1]\\), choose the adjacent points \\(g_-\\leq d\\leq g_+\\) of \\(\\Gamma_M\\) and randomize between them so that the randomized action \\(G\\) has mean \\(d\\).  Since \\(g_+-g_-=1/M\\),\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Var}(G)\\leq\\frac{(g_+-g_-)^2}{4}\n=\\frac1{4M^2}.\n\\]\nFor every target value \\(\\tau\\),\n\\[\n\\mathbb E(G-\\tau)^2=(d-\\tau)^2+\\operatorname{Var}(G)\n\\leq(d-\\tau)^2+\\frac1{4M^2}.\n\\]\nApply this replacement independently at each finite observation orbit \\((r,x)\\), and then take the same maxima and minima as in the two orbit games.  This proves both right inequalities, including cells of zero likelihood because the construction is defined on every cell.",
